IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tco-dates`
IMPORT `tco-rules`
IMPORT `tco-seat`

-- Coroners Act 1995 (Tas) -- worked cases for the family's questions (tco-seat.l4), the dates (tco-dates.l4) and the
-- regulative rules (tco-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from
-- the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are
-- illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`nd` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `the date` 14 `days after` (`d` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 17 3 2026
#ASSERT `the date` 14 `days after` (`d` 20 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 5 3 2028
#ASSERT `the anniversary` 1 `years after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the moment` (`d` 2 1 2026) `at` 0 `h` 0 MINUS `the moment` (`d` 1 1 2026) `at` 0 `h` 0 EQUALS 1440
#ASSERT `the moment` (`d` 1 1 2026) `at` 10 `h` 30 MINUS `the moment` (`d` 1 1 2026) `at` 9 `h` 15 EQUALS 75

§§ `s 3A -- senior next of kin`

-- Helper: someone not a spouse, with only the "available" facts varying.
GIVEN `rel` IS A `Relationship to the deceased`, `adult` IS A BOOLEAN, `sp` IS A BOOLEAN, `ch` IS A BOOLEAN, `cp` IS A BOOLEAN, `pa` IS A BOOLEAN, `si` IS A BOOLEAN, `same` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Senior next of kin answer`
`kin` `rel` `adult` `sp` `ch` `cp` `pa` `si` `same` MEANS
    `Am I the senior next of kin` `rel` `adult` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `sp` `ch` `cp` `pa` `si` `same` FALSE FALSE

-- The only spouse: (a).
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `the spouse or significant-relationship partner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
-- Two surviving spouses; I was the last to qualify: (b).
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `the spouse or significant-relationship partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
-- Two surviving spouses; I was the earlier; the last is not available and approves me: (c).
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `the spouse or significant-relationship partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
-- The same, but the last spouse is available.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `the spouse or significant-relationship partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`
-- The same, last spouse not available but does not approve.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `the spouse or significant-relationship partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`
-- Three spouses; two earlier ones both approved while the last is unavailable: equally placed.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `the spouse or significant-relationship partner` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are one of several people equally placed to be the senior next of kin`
-- A former partner, not a spouse immediately before the death, and only one spouse survived.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `the spouse or significant-relationship partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`
-- An adult child, no spouse available, no other child: (d).
#ASSERT `kin` `a child` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
-- An adult child, spouse available.
#ASSERT `kin` `a child` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin: someone ranked above you is available`
-- A child of 17.
#ASSERT `kin` `a child` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`
-- One of three adult children.
#ASSERT `kin` `a child` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `you are one of several people equally placed to be the senior next of kin`
-- An adult child when a parent is available: a parent ranks lower.
#ASSERT `kin` `a child` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
-- The registered caring partner, adult child available.
#ASSERT `kin` `the partner in a registered caring relationship` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin: someone ranked above you is available`
-- The registered caring partner, no spouse or adult child: (e) (singular: no tie).
#ASSERT `kin` `the partner in a registered caring relationship` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
-- A parent, the other parent also available: equally placed (f).
#ASSERT `kin` `a parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `you are one of several people equally placed to be the senior next of kin`
-- A parent when only a child under 18 survives (the child is not an "adult child available").
#ASSERT `kin` `a parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
-- A parent, caring partner available.
#ASSERT `kin` `a parent` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin: someone ranked above you is available`
-- An adult sibling, parent available.
#ASSERT `kin` `a sibling` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin: someone ranked above you is available`
-- An adult sibling, nobody above: (g).
#ASSERT `kin` `a sibling` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
-- A sibling of 17.
#ASSERT `kin` `a sibling` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`
-- The executor, adult sibling available.
#ASSERT `kin` `an executor or personal representative` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin: someone ranked above you is available`
-- The executor, nobody above: (h).
#ASSERT `kin` `an executor or personal representative` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
-- A friend.
#ASSERT `kin` `none of these` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`
-- The appropriate person by Aboriginal custom, not otherwise ranked: (i).
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `none of these` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `you may be the senior next of kin as the appropriate person by Aboriginal custom`
-- A sibling who is also the appropriate person, a parent available: (i).
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `a sibling` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `you may be the senior next of kin as the appropriate person by Aboriginal custom`
-- The only spouse, who is also the appropriate person: (a) answers first (fork F8).
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `the spouse or significant-relationship partner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `you are the senior next of kin`
-- Appropriate by custom, but the deceased was not Aboriginal.
#ASSERT `Am I the senior next of kin` `none of these` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `you are not the senior next of kin on these facts`

-- s 3B
#ASSERT `Can I appeal who is the senior next of kin` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal who is the senior next of kin` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal who is the senior next of kin` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 3 -- reportable death`

-- A fall from scaffolding in Hobart.
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `at work, or from an accident or injury at work, and not apparently from natural causes` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A road crash in Victoria, body flown home, Tasmanian resident: body in Tasmania (a)(i).
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `unexpected, unnatural or violent, or from an accident or injury` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same crash, body stays in Victoria, cause certified there: none of (a), (b).
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `unexpected, unnatural or violent, or from an accident or injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A Tasmanian resident dies in Bali of an illness, no local doctor certifies the cause: (b).
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `an expected death from natural causes, none of the above` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An expected death from cancer in a Launceston hospice.
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `an expected death from natural causes, none of the above` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Died on the ferry to Tasmania after an unexpected collapse: (a)(iiia).
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `unexpected, unnatural or violent, or from an accident or injury` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Died while escaping custody interstate, no Tasmanian connection: (c) needs none.
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `while escaping or attempting to escape from custody` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Died while being detained: (d).
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `while being detained by a police, correctional or mental health officer or prescribed person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Unexpected death after surgery in Tasmania: (a)(v).
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `during or after a medical procedure, and not reasonably expected` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- SUDI in Tasmania: (a)(viii).
#ASSERT `Is it a reportable death` `sudden and unexpected death of a child under one` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 19 -- reporting`

#ASSERT `Must I report the death` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you must report the death as soon as possible to a coroner or a police officer`
-- Believe it has already been reported.
#ASSERT `Must I report the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 19 does not require you to report it`
-- No reasonable grounds to think it reportable.
#ASSERT `Must I report the death` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 19 does not require you to report it`
-- A family member of a prisoner who died in custody.
#ASSERT `Must I report the death` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 19 does not require you to report it`
-- The prison officer in whose custody the person died.
#ASSERT `Must I report the death` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `you must report the death as soon as possible to a coroner`
-- The second doctor at the bedside.
#ASSERT `Must I report the death` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `you need not report it, but must give the coroner any information that may help`

§§ `ss 27, 37, 42 -- asking the coroner`

#ASSERT `Can I ask the coroner` `an inquest into a death` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I ask the coroner` `an inquest into a death` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I ask the coroner` `an autopsy` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I ask the coroner` `an autopsy` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Fire: the coroner's jurisdiction over a death is irrelevant.
#ASSERT `Can I ask the coroner` `an investigation into a fire or explosion` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 21-26A -- the inquest`

-- Helper: jurisdiction, nothing special, Tasmanian connection, with the heads varying.
GIVEN `homicide` IS A BOOLEAN, `custody` IS A BOOLEAN, `work` IS A BOOLEAN, `not natural` IS A BOOLEAN, `asked` IS A BOOLEAN, `satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Inquest answer`
`inquest` `homicide` `custody` `work` `not natural` `asked` `satisfied` MEANS
    `Must there be an inquest` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `homicide` `custody` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `work` `not natural` `asked` `satisfied`

#ASSERT `inquest` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`
#ASSERT `inquest` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`
-- A death at work the coroner is not satisfied was natural: (ea).
#ASSERT `inquest` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held as a workplace death, but the senior next of kin may ask the coroner not to hold it`
-- The family asked in time and the coroner is satisfied: s 26A(3).
#ASSERT `inquest` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the coroner may decline to hold the workplace death inquest`
-- Asked, but the coroner is not satisfied.
#ASSERT `inquest` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held as a workplace death, but the senior next of kin may ask the coroner not to hold it`
-- Workplace death and homicide suspected: s 26A lifts only (ea).
#ASSERT `inquest` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`
-- Died at work, coroner satisfied it was natural (a heart attack at the desk).
#ASSERT `inquest` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no inquest is required, but one may be held if the coroner or Chief Magistrate considers it desirable`
#ASSERT `inquest` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no inquest is required, but one may be held if the coroner or Chief Magistrate considers it desirable`
-- No jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquest` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner has no jurisdiction to investigate this death`
-- Aboriginal remains.
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquest` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act no longer applies: the remains are Aboriginal remains`
-- An inquest in Victoria, no direction.
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquest` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner need not investigate: there is an investigation or inquest in another State or Territory`
-- An inquest in Victoria, the Attorney-General directs one here.
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquest` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`
-- Homicide suspected but no Tasmanian connection.
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquest` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no inquest is required, but one may be held if the coroner or Chief Magistrate considers it desirable`
-- The Chief Magistrate directs.
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquest` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`
-- Unknown identity.
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquest` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an inquest must be held`

§§ `s 25 -- adjournment`

#ASSERT `Is the inquest adjourned for the criminal case` `causing the death by dangerous driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the inquest must be adjourned until the criminal proceedings conclude`
#ASSERT `Is the inquest adjourned for the criminal case` `causing the death by dangerous driving` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 25 does not require the inquest to be adjourned`
#ASSERT `Is the inquest adjourned for the criminal case` `another offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 25 does not require the inquest to be adjourned`
-- Told only after the finding.
#ASSERT `Is the inquest adjourned for the criminal case` `manslaughter of the deceased` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 25 does not require the inquest to be adjourned`
#ASSERT `Is the inquest adjourned for the criminal case` `manslaughter of the deceased` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the coroner may resume the inquest as a fresh inquest`
#ASSERT `Is the inquest adjourned for the criminal case` `manslaughter of the deceased` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the coroner may not resume the inquest and must tell the Attorney-General`
#ASSERT `Is the inquest adjourned for the criminal case` `unlawfully causing the fire` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the inquest must be adjourned until the criminal proceedings conclude`
-- Not charged before justices (yet).
#ASSERT `Is the inquest adjourned for the criminal case` `murder of the deceased` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 25 does not require the inquest to be adjourned`

§§ `s 52 -- at the inquest`

#ASSERT `Can I take part in the inquest this way` TRUE `in person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I take part in the inquest this way` TRUE `by an Australian legal practitioner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I take part in the inquest this way` TRUE `by another person, with the coroner's permission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I take part in the inquest this way` TRUE `by another person, without the coroner's permission` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I take part in the inquest this way` FALSE `by an Australian legal practitioner` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 29, 46, 54, 64 -- evidence`

#ASSERT `Can I use it in my court case` `the coroner's record of a death investigation, as proof of the facts in it` `a civil proceeding` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I use it in my court case` `the coroner's record of a fire or explosion investigation, as proof of the facts in it` `a civil proceeding` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The employer's manager's evidence at the inquest, in the family's damages claim against the employer's manager.
#ASSERT `Can I use it in my court case` `what a witness said giving evidence at the inquest, against that witness` `a civil proceeding` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I use it in my court case` `what a witness said giving evidence at the inquest, against that witness` `a criminal proceeding other than for perjury` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I use it in my court case` `what a witness said giving evidence at the inquest, against that witness` `a prosecution of the witness for perjury in giving that evidence` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I use it in my court case` `what a witness said giving evidence at the inquest, against someone else` `a civil proceeding` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I use it in my court case` `making the coroner give evidence of what the coroner learned in the investigation` `a civil proceeding` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `The 14-day steps`

`sc` MEANS `apply to the Supreme Court for an inquest the coroner or Chief Magistrate decided not to hold`
`wp` MEANS `ask the coroner in writing not to hold a workplace death inquest`
`rq` MEANS `apply to the Supreme Court for the inquest I asked for and was refused`
`fe` MEANS `apply to the Supreme Court for the fire or explosion inquest I asked for and was refused`

-- Notice received 3 March 2026: the 14th day after is 17 March.
#ASSERT `What is the last day for my 14-day step` `sc` TRUE FALSE (`d` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `you may take this step up to and including` (`d` 17 3 2026)
#ASSERT `What is the last day for my 14-day step` `wp` TRUE FALSE (`d` 25 12 2026) EQUALS `you may take this step up to and including` (`d` 8 1 2027)
#ASSERT `What is the last day for my 14-day step` `rq` FALSE TRUE (`d` 20 2 2028) EQUALS `you may take this step up to and including` (`d` 5 3 2028)
#ASSERT `What is the last day for my 14-day step` `sc` FALSE TRUE (`d` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `this step is not open to you`
#ASSERT `What is the last day for my 14-day step` `fe` FALSE FALSE (`d` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `this step is not open to you`
#ASSERT `What is the last day for my 14-day step` `fe` FALSE TRUE (`d` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `you may take this step up to and including` (`d` 17 3 2026)

#ASSERT `Can I still take my 14-day step on this day` `sc` TRUE FALSE (`d` 3 3 2026) (`d` 17 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still take my 14-day step on this day` `sc` TRUE FALSE (`d` 3 3 2026) (`d` 18 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still take my 14-day step on this day` `sc` TRUE FALSE (`d` 3 3 2026) (`d` 3 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still take my 14-day step on this day` `sc` TRUE FALSE (`d` 3 3 2026) (`d` 2 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still take my 14-day step on this day` `wp` TRUE FALSE (`d` 25 12 2026) (`d` 8 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still take my 14-day step on this day` `wp` TRUE FALSE (`d` 25 12 2026) (`d` 9 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still take my 14-day step on this day` `wp` FALSE TRUE (`d` 25 12 2026) (`d` 26 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I still take my 14-day step on this day` `rq` FALSE TRUE (`d` 20 2 2028) (`d` 5 3 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still take my 14-day step on this day` `rq` FALSE TRUE (`d` 20 2 2028) (`d` 6 3 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still take my 14-day step on this day` `fe` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `The 48-hour applications`

`au` MEANS `apply to the Supreme Court for the autopsy I asked for and was refused`
`na` MEANS `apply to the Supreme Court for an order that no autopsy be performed`
`ex` MEANS `apply to the Supreme Court for an order that the body not be exhumed`

-- Notice at 14:30 on 10 March 2026: the 48 hours end at 14:30 on 12 March.
