§§ `s 58C -- the records`

`pm` MEANS `a pathology or autopsy report by the State Forensic Pathologist or an approved pathologist or practitioner`

-- Request 5 January 2026: 28 days after is 2 February.
#ASSERT `Must I be given a copy of the record` TRUE TRUE `pm` TRUE `no ground for refusal` (`d` 5 1 2026) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `you must be given a copy by` (`d` 2 2 2026)
-- An agreed later day.
#ASSERT `Must I be given a copy of the record` TRUE TRUE `a transcript or recording of oral evidence` TRUE `no ground for refusal` (`d` 5 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `you must be given a copy by` (`d` 1 3 2026)
-- Request 15 February 2028 (leap year): 14 March.
#ASSERT `Must I be given a copy of the record` TRUE TRUE `pm` TRUE `no ground for refusal` (`d` 15 2 2028) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `you must be given a copy by` (`d` 14 3 2028)
#ASSERT `Must I be given a copy of the record` TRUE TRUE `pm` TRUE `an unreasonable intrusion on another person's privacy, contrary to the public interest` (`d` 5 1 2026) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `the authority may refuse, or give you a redacted or modified copy`
#ASSERT `Must I be given a copy of the record` TRUE TRUE `pm` TRUE `likely to prejudice an investigation, law enforcement or a fair trial` (`d` 5 1 2026) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `the authority may refuse, or give you a redacted or modified copy`
#ASSERT `Must I be given a copy of the record` TRUE TRUE `some other document` TRUE `no ground for refusal` (`d` 5 1 2026) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `this is not a coronial record`
